The short question:

What are the penalties for killing your pet, and what do you need to
do to overcome them?

The long story that led up to the short question:

I'm playing a rogue, 9th level, in Minetown, with two dogs and a
kitten as pets. I test a "message disappears" wand by zapping it at a
scroll I don't want. Nothing happens to the scroll, but my kitten (a
diagonal move away) becomes invisible. So now I know that my wand is
invisibility, and as I don't have "see invisible," I have to be
careful not to charge into it.

A little later on, I start using my wand of create monster at the
(coaligned) temple. My very first sacrifice yields (drum roll
please)... Sting! (*&$&*&$*% Kos!) So I'm creating monsters and
saccing to get rid of my prayer timeout and see if I can get a BETTER
gift, when I create a nymph. One wants to stay a bit of a distance
away, so I fire daggers at her from across the room.

"It yowls! You killed it! You hear the rumble of distant thunder..."

Now, from what I thought I remembered, I've angered Kos (not merely
displeased him) and I'll never be able to pray again unless I can
mollify him (and I've heard the horror stories of trying to mollify an
angry chaotic god). I save and go into wizmode to see what I may have
done.

Wizmode seems to tell me that I've taken a -15 alignment hit, a -1
luck penalty, and I can not safely pray. A couple thousand turns, a
blessed luckstone wish, and many kills (but no sacs) later, my wizmode
hero has a positive alignment and +3 luck (indicating that the luck
penalty had timed out), but still cannot safely pray. Just what I'd
feared. Kos's anger ain't gonna time out.

Opening up my main game again, I wander around a bit in the lower
levels of the mines and find a gray stone. It kicks across the room,
so it isn't a loadstone. I rub a dagger on it, and it doesn't go
"scritch, scritch," so it isn't a touchstone.  I pick it up, take it
back to minetown, and the general store proprietor is willing to part
with 30 Z for it. Yaay, a luckstone, and I didn't even have to go to
the bottom of the mines.

My dogs having taught a lesson to the minetown guard, I begin dipping
potions for water--I'd better be able to farm my holy water, cause I'm
not gonna be able to pray for it, right? "An endless stream of snakes
pours forth!" I get two snake corpses. They seem paltry gifts to offer
to an angry god, but what have I got to lose. I offer the first.

"Your sacrifice is consumed in a burst of flame! A four-leaf clover
appears at your feet."

Huh? Kos isn't mad anymore? I offer the second.

"Your sacrifice is consumed in a burst of flame! An object appears at
your feet. 'Use my gift wisely!'
A - a morningstar named Trollsbane."

Okay, so Kos hasn't gotten much less stingy with his gifts, but
still... why isn't he mad? It must've been less than 500 turns between
killing the kitten and offering the snake. I didn't kill that many
monsters. What gives?

(Thinking about it now, maybe my wizmode testing was in error because
it was the start of a new game. Maybe I hadn't killed enough monsters
to be able to pray in the first place yet?)
